  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advocacy for Endangered Areas in the Bethlehem Governorate</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to protect endangered areas in Bethlehem from annexation and forced displacement.  It is focused on 5 areas of Bethlehem Governorate that are particularly threatened and central to the economy and/or Palestinian Christian cultural identity.  It will increase international awareness and advocacy through a comprehensive approach that includes collecting data and testimonies from residents then producing a baseline advocacy report, fact sheets, infographics, and a podcast. These materials will inform and mobilize key international actors - diplomatic missions, UN organisations, regional bodies, civil society &amp; church-affiliated organisations, and the general public about the severity of the immediate annexation threats.  It will shed light on the specific detrimental impacts that recently-passed measures are having on Bethlehem in the context of an increasing fragmentation of the Palestinian Christian population.  The partner will also make two submissions to UN Special Procedures addressing human rights violations such as restrictions on movement, religious freedom, land confiscation &amp; annexation, and the broader impact on the community.</narrative>
  </description>
